{
 "_readme": [
  "Hubs for the OpenStreetMap civic-amenity pull (mapsee_ingest_osm_amenities.py).",
  "Same shape as osm_food_sources.json and osm_secondhand_sources.json: a centre",
  "and a radius in miles, one entry per metro, tiled by the ingest at TILE_DEG.",
  "",
  "MOST OF WHAT THIS RETURNS IS FURNITURE, and that is the design rather than a",
  "shortfall. A drinking fountain has nothing to say beyond being a drinking",
  "fountain; the pin says it and the row is marked pin_only, so it is drawn and",
  "never listed, indexed or opened. The listing/furniture split is printed per",
  "area on every run - a run that adds only furniture has still made the map",
  "more useful, and being able to SEE that is the point of printing both.",
  "",
  "AREA SHAPE IS area_bbox's, NOT THIS FILE'S CHOICE. It reads area['center'] as a [lat, lon] PAIR (or an explicit 'bbox'), and radius_miles. Writing lat/lon as separate keys parses as JSON, matches every test that builds a NormalizedEvent directly, and dies with KeyError: 'center' on the first real run - which is exactly what it did. test_ingest_osm_amenities.py now runs every area in this file through area_bbox.",
  "",
  "260 AREAS, AND THEY ARE THE METROS MAPSEE ALREADY SWEEPS FOR EVENTS.",
  "Generated 2026-09-20 from metros_us.txt + metros_global.json, the one list",
  "every US and international event sweep reads, deduped against what was here",
  "by name AND by proximity (under 12 miles is the same place: 'Portland OR' is",
  "the 'Portland' that was already configured). Amenities only pay off where",
  "somebody is looking, so the event metros are exactly the right list.",
  "",
  "A US area carries its state CODE and an international one carries no region,",
  "which is the convention the first ten set. The codes were reverse-geocoded",
  "once, at config-build time, from each centre - 78 of 78 resolved. They are",
  "not derived at ingest: `region` lands on every row, and a wrong one is worse",
  "than none. The CITY on a row never comes from here, it comes from the",
  "element's own addr:city - see the note in mapsee_ingest_osm_food.to_event.",
  "",
  "THE MATRIX IS SHARDED BY WEEK, because GitHub caps a matrix at 256 jobs and",
  "this file holds 260 areas - the whole list in one run would not be slow, it",
  "would fail to start. osm-amenities.yml takes every Nth area, five shards, a",
  "full turn every five weeks. Adding areas here is free until the shard size",
  "(64) is exceeded, at which point the turn simply gets longer."
 ],
